# AMFV security decoder (from SECURITY-CHECK, prism.zil):
#   answer = OUTER[(2 * color_index + inner_index) mod 32]
#
# Colors (index): WHITE 0, DARK GREEN 1, DARK BLUE 2, PINK 3,
#   ORANGE 4, PURPLE 5, TAN 6, AQUA 7, LIGHT BLUE 8, LIGHT GREEN 9,
#   LIGHT GRAY 10, YELLOW 11, BLACK 12, DARK GRAY 13, BROWN 14, RED 15
#
# INNER (find the shown number's index):
#   89 61 50 18 29 82 46 77 27 68 22 95 40 58 15 86
#   28 33 94 11 64 98 34 49 60 16 85 52 37 53 93 91
#
# OUTER (read the answer at the computed index):
#   12 66 73 36 90 41 19 48 62 92 55 23 84 99 57 20
#   78 67 51 88 17 31 70 39 96 25 81 83 47 54 13 43
#
# Example, if you are asked for: YELLOW 86
# That will be 41
# (YELLOW is color 11; 86 sits at inner index 15; 2×11+15 = 37, wraps
# to 5; outer[5] = 41.)

>
wait
wait
wait
