# The feeder is real; it's just on a delivery schedule. Emily
# Warren's message is sent by I-MESSAGE-Z, which then re-queues
# itself for 274 minutes -- her "four or five hours" -- and only
# that second firing moves the hardware into the interface room.
# Every prior attempt failed simply because the ports list was
# checked before the truck arrived. The win itself (prism.zil:3766)
# needs three things at transmit time: the transmitter on, the
# record buffer as the feed, and at least two beats of Ryder's
# rant in that buffer -- the recording above banked all five. Once
# "Now transmitting record buffer" prints, I-WIN is queued thirteen
# minutes out and Ryder's career is over.

